# Every setting kotogen reads, with what it does. Read it, and copy the lines
# you need.
#
#   THE API KEYS go into a ".env" at the root of the repository (already in
#   .gitignore): copy there the key lines you need, the first three below.
#   Without that file, or without a repository, the menu writes the keys into
#   "secrets.env" in the configuration folder, with mode 0600.
#
#   THE SETTINGS go into "settings.env" in the configuration folder:
#       Linux   ~/.config/kotogen/settings.env   (or $XDG_CONFIG_HOME)
#       macOS   ~/Library/Application Support/kotogen/settings.env
#       Windows %APPDATA%\kotogen\settings.env
#   The interactive menu writes that file itself; this one only lists what
#   exists and what it does.
#
# A setting you wrote by hand into the ".env" keeps applying from there, and the
# menu updates it in that file rather than writing a second copy elsewhere.
# A variable exported in your shell (export
# KOTOGEN_MODEL=... in a ~/.bashrc) wins over both files, at every launch.

# ── OpenRouter (the default provider - every model behind one key, no extra
#    package) ──
#    The "k" setting of the interactive menu asks for this key and records it;
#    so does a command that finds no key.
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=sk-or-...

# ── Native Anthropic (optional): for the anthropic provider only ──
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...

# ── Native OpenAI (optional): for the openai provider only ──
# OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...

# ── AI model: what is called without --provider / --model ──
#    None is built in: models come and go faster than releases. The "m" setting
#    of the interactive menu lists what each provider serves today (the
#    OpenRouter catalogue with its prices, the models Anthropic and OpenAI
#    serve to your key) and writes these two lines. The price varies by a
#    factor of ten from one model to the next, and so does the result.
#    KOTOGEN_MODEL only applies to the provider below: an explicit, different
#    --provider needs its own --model.
# KOTOGEN_PROVIDER=openrouter
# KOTOGEN_MODEL=

# ── Interface language (optional): en (default), fr, ja. The "l" setting of
#    the menu lists them. Every language but English is a table under
#    src/kotogen/locales/; a sentence a table lacks shows in English.
#
#    The language the CARDS are written in is a separate setting, English by
#    default too: all.lang, kept in templates.env with the other choices about
#    the cards. The "g" setting of the menu, right under "l", changes it. ──
# KOTOGEN_LANG=fr

# ── Getting started (optional): the guide the assistant opens on its first
#    launch in a terminal, if the AI key, the model, Anki or a note type is
#    missing, with one page per step: the languages, the key, the model,
#    AnkiConnect and the note types, the optional modules. That first launch
#    writes this line itself, whether the guide opened or not; delete the line
#    and the next launch counts as the first again. ──
# KOTOGEN_GETTING_STARTED=0

# ── Display currency (optional): OpenRouter bills in dollars, and the costs
#    can be shown in another currency, converted at the day's ECB rate (a
#    public endpoint with no key, cached for a day). The "c" setting of the
#    interactive menu picks the currency and writes this line: EUR, JPY, GBP,
#    CHF, SEK... In dollars (the default), no request is made. ──
# KOTOGEN_CURRENCY=EUR
#
#    A fixed rate instead of the day's (for an expense report, or accounts kept
#    by hand): how many units of the currency one dollar is worth.
# KOTOGEN_CURRENCY_RATE=0.86

# ── Optional modules (optional): ask (default), always, never.
#    The core of the program runs without them. Each of these needs its own
#    package: the pages of a PDF as images, Whisper transcription, the NHK
#    capture, YouTube videos, and the native Anthropic and OpenAI providers.
#    "ask" offers the missing ones all at once on the first launch in a
#    terminal, once per environment, and remembers the answer; "always"
#    installs whatever is missing without asking, at every launch, which is
#    also how to retry after a failure; "never" installs nothing. In all three
#    cases, a command that needs a missing package says which one to install.
#    FFmpeg is a system package and is never installed this way. ──
# KOTOGEN_INSTALL=always

# ── Output (optional): the folder of the TSV and MP3 files produced
#    (default: the folder the command is run from) ──
#    The "o" setting of the interactive menu offers the usual folders (current
#    folder, Desktop, Downloads, Documents) and writes this line. It asks the
#    system where those folders are: Windows may redirect them to OneDrive, and
#    on Linux they are named in the session language (~/Bureau, ~/Escritorio).
# KOTOGEN_OUTPUT_DIR=C:\Users\me\anki_output
# KOTOGEN_OUTPUT_DIR=/home/me/anki_output

# ── Auto-send (optional): the cards go into Anki without a question, and the
#    TSV is only a backup kept in the cache. --no-send turns it off for one
#    run; the "s" key of the interactive settings toggles it and records it. ──
# KOTOGEN_AUTO_SEND=1

# ── File format (optional): tsv (default), json. The TSV is what Anki
#    imports; json writes JSON Lines instead (a header line, then one card per
#    line with its identity, its fields, its tags and its media) for a tool
#    other than Anki, and sends nothing. --format overrides it for one run. ──
# KOTOGEN_FORMAT=json

# ── Audio compression (optional): none (default), light (MP3 mono 96k),
#    medium (64k), strong (48k), from the most faithful to the lightest. With
#    none, the site's stream is copied as it is where possible, and a passage
#    cut out of a file is re-encoded at 192k. --audio-quality overrides it; the
#    "q" key of the interactive settings cycles through the four and records
#    it. ──
# KOTOGEN_AUDIO_QUALITY=strong

# ── Video picture (optional): ask (default), always, never.
#    "ask" asks once per command, and only if a video is involved. Keeping the
#    picture cuts each passage as a video clip (VP9/WebM 480p) that the card
#    plays; sound only makes an ordinary listening card. A passage longer than
#    90 seconds falls back to sound only, without a message. Outside a
#    terminal, or with --yes, the question answers itself with sound only.
#    --video / --no-video override it; the "i" key of the interactive settings
#    cycles through the three and records it. ──
# KOTOGEN_VIDEO=always

# ── Doubtful cards (optional): ask (default), keep, tag, drop. These are the
#    cards the model returned damaged, the ones marked "!!" in the output: a
#    translation without the line count of the text, a missing transcript, the
#    right answer repeated among the decoys. They are worth keeping (the
#    question stands, and they are paid for) but need checking.
#    "keep" exports them as they are; "tag" exports them with a `Check::...`
#    tag, which finds them in Anki (`tag:Check::*`) and is removed in one step
#    once they are checked; "drop" leaves them out of the file AND out of the
#    deck; "ask" asks once, just before sending, and only if there are any.
#    Outside a terminal, or with --yes, the question answers itself by tagging
#    them, since nobody read the "!!" lines. --proofread overrides it; the "p"
#    key of the interactive settings cycles through the four and records it. ──
# KOTOGEN_PROOFREAD=keep

# ── Media folder (optional): only if kotogen cannot find the collection.media
#    folder (Anki closed, and a profile outside the usual place). Looked for
#    by default in %APPDATA%\Anki2 on Windows, ~/.local/share/Anki2 on Linux
#    (and the net.ankiweb.Anki Flatpak), and
#    ~/Library/Application Support/Anki2 on macOS. ──
# KOTOGEN_MEDIA_DIR=C:\Users\me\AppData\Roaming\Anki2\User 1\collection.media
# KOTOGEN_MEDIA_DIR=/home/me/.local/share/Anki2/User 1/collection.media

# ── Connection to AnkiConnect (optional): the add-on listens on
#    http://127.0.0.1:8765 by default. These two lines are only needed if its
#    configuration was changed (in Anki: Tools > Add-ons > AnkiConnect >
#    Config, fields webBindAddress, webBindPort, apiKey).
#
#    Where the add-on listens, if not on the default port. The scheme is
#    optional ("127.0.0.1:8766" is enough). Write 127.0.0.1 rather than
#    "localhost": on Windows, localhost costs two seconds per request, the time
#    the IPv6 loopback takes to refuse the connection. An address on another
#    machine does not receive the media: kotogen hands each media file to Anki
#    by its local path, and Anki reads it from there. ──
# KOTOGEN_ANKICONNECT_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8766
#
#    The key, if the add-on's "apiKey" setting requires one. Without it, Anki
#    answers but refuses every request; the menu says so.
# KOTOGEN_ANKICONNECT_KEY=...

# ── Backup (optional): kotogen takes a snapshot of the decks (fields, tags,
#    card scheduling, templates) before "maintain", at the first write of
#    "kotogen ask", and before "deck install" rewrites a note type. The
#    commands that only add cards take none. ──
#
#    Turn the automatic backup off ("kotogen backup" run by hand still works,
#    and "kotogen backup --restore" still backs up what it overwrites):
# KOTOGEN_BACKUP=0
#
#    Keep the backups somewhere other than the platform's data folder
#    (%LOCALAPPDATA%\kotogen\backups on Windows, ~/.local/share/kotogen/backups
#    on Linux, ~/Library/Application Support/kotogen/backups on macOS):
# KOTOGEN_BACKUP_DIR=C:\Users\me\backups\kotogen
# KOTOGEN_BACKUP_DIR=/home/me/backups/kotogen

# ── Verbose mode (optional): at the end of a command, the interactive
#    assistant prints the equivalent command line, to help you learn the CLI.
#    The "v" key of the interactive settings toggles it and records it. ──
# KOTOGEN_VERBOSE=1

# ── Diagnostics (optional): print the full traceback of an unexpected error
#    instead of a one-line summary. Also prints the provider's answer when it
#    refuses a call (key, credit, rights), and what the model says between the
#    steps of "kotogen ask". ──
# KOTOGEN_DEBUG=1

# ── Menus (optional): numbered input instead of arrow-key navigation, for a
#    terminal that shows special keys or redraws badly. ──
# KOTOGEN_NO_RAW_KEYS=1

# ── What YOUR profile installs (optional) ──
#    The repository holds every note type and card, including the ones you do
#    not review. These settings choose what you install; the rest is ignored,
#    without being removed from the repository.
#
#    The cards wanted from a note type (an allow-list, comma separated).
#    Unset, every card of the note type is installed. Example: reviewing
#    vocabulary from Japanese only (Recognition), without "deck install"
#    offering Production on every run. One variable per command, on the same
#    pattern; the card names are those of the note type in Anki.
# KOTOGEN_KANJI_CARDS=
# KOTOGEN_VOCAB_CARDS=Recognition
# KOTOGEN_GRAMMAR_CARDS=
# KOTOGEN_AUDIO_CARDS=
# KOTOGEN_READING_CARDS=
#
#    Commands you do not use: their entry leaves the menu, and "deck install"
#    and the backups skip them unless --only names them. "kotogen grammar"
#    typed in full still works.
# KOTOGEN_SKIP=grammar,audio

# ── Decks and note types (optional): override the default names. The names
#    are English in every language of the cards: they are the schema of your
#    collection, not text. Set yours BEFORE the first "deck install": changing
#    a note type's name afterwards points kotogen at another type, and the
#    notes stay in the old one. ──
# KOTOGEN_KANJI_DECK=Japanese::Kanji
# KOTOGEN_KANJI_NOTETYPE=Kanji
# KOTOGEN_VOCAB_DECK=Japanese::Vocabulary
# KOTOGEN_VOCAB_NOTETYPE=Vocabulary
# KOTOGEN_GRAMMAR_DECK=Japanese::Grammar
# KOTOGEN_GRAMMAR_NOTETYPE=Grammar
# KOTOGEN_AUDIO_DECK=Japanese::Listening
# KOTOGEN_AUDIO_NOTETYPE=Listening
# KOTOGEN_READING_DECK=Japanese::Reading
# KOTOGEN_READING_NOTETYPE=Reading

# ── What the flags of maintain ask for, where it differs from the default
#    (red=error orange=simplify green=enrich blue=text pink=derive
#    turquoise=duplicate purple=audio, star: nothing). An action answers one
#    flag at most; none = the flag is left alone, and leech=none leaves the
#    leeches alone. Also in the menu: Corrections > Marks. ──
# KOTOGEN_FLAGS=pink=renew,star=derive
